(APPELLATE LITIGATION BRIEFING PACKET AND RISK ASSESSMENT) '
() '
(Case Ref: In re Commercial Licensing Dispute | Circuit Court of) '
(Appeals) '
() '
(1. PROCEDURAL POSTURE AND JURISDICTIONAL BASIS) '
() '
(This litigation memorandum evaluates the legal posture of) '
(appellant's interlocutory appeal from a district court order) '
(granting preliminary injunctive relief under 28 U.S.C. 1292\(a\)\(1\).) '
(Appellant contends that the lower court abused its discretion by) '
(enjoining enforcement of non-compete covenants across 14 sovereign) '
(states.) '
() '
(Appellate jurisdiction is founded upon timely notice of appeal filed) '
(within thirty days of docket entry. The standard of review applied) '
(by the circuit court is de novo for conclusions of law, abuse of) '
(discretion for injunctive balance determinations, and clear error) '
(for underlying findings of fact.) '
() '
(2. FOUR-FACTOR PRELIMINARY INJUNCTION ANALYSIS) '
() '
(Under controlling Supreme Court precedent \(Winter v. Natural) '
(Resources Defense Council\), a plaintiff seeking preliminary) '
(injunctive relief must establish: \(a\) likelihood of success on the) '
(merits; \(b\) irreparable harm absent an injunction; \(c\) the balance) '
(of equities tips in their favor; and \(d\) the public interest favors) '
(relief.) '
() '
ET

endstream
