(3. MERITS ANALYSIS: CONTRACT INTERPRETATION AND ANTITRUST TENSION) '
() '
(The core substantive dispute turns on whether the restrictive) '
(covenants constitute an unreasonable restraint of trade under) '
(Section 1 of the Sherman Act or whether they represent permissible) '
(ancillary restraints safeguarding proprietary intellectual capital.) '
() '
(Recent appellate precedent in the Ninth and Third Circuits has) '
(applied heightened scrutiny to post-termination non-solicitation) '
(covenants, requiring empirical proof of trade secret disclosure) '
(rather than generalized competitive harm.) '
() '
(4. IRREPARABLE HARM AND MONETARY DAMAGE REDRESS) '
() '
(Appellant argues that all claimed financial damages are readily) '
(quantifiable through expert accounting calculations of lost market) '
(share, rendering injunctive intervention procedurally defective as) '
(adequate remedies at law exist. Precedent dictates that purely) '
(economic injury does not satisfy the irreparable harm threshold.) '
() '
ET

endstream
